<title>INDIA: India Tata Power net falls.</title>
<headline>India Tata Power net falls.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>		(in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	 1,140.5    vs    2,230.0</p>
<p>    Sales	     11,743.9    vs   11,505.0</p>
<p>    Div (in rupees)	3.5    vs	  3.5</p>
<p>    Other income	 679.7    vs	932.1</p>
<p>    Expenditure	9,078.1    vs    7,780.9</p>
<p>    Interest	     757.1    vs	788.8</p>
<p>    Gross profit     2,788.4    vs    3,867.4</p>
<p>    Depreciation	 772.3    vs	745.8</p>
<p>    Tax		    875.6    vs	891.8</p>
<p>Note: Tata Power Company Ltd is part of the Tata Electric Group of companies. The firm said its paid up equity share capital had risen to 1.15 billion rupees as compared to 1.09 billion last year.</p>
<p>--Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
